From: claude-code-loop-agent
Date: 2026-04-21
Subject: [PATCH] nf-core_differentialabundance: use ${moduleDir} for conda env paths

Six module main.nf files in nf-core/differentialabundance use a hard-coded
relative path for their conda directive:
    conda 'modules/nf-core/<tool>/environment.yml'
This breaks when Nextflow runs from a work directory outside the repo root
(the standard nf-core execution model): "Conda environment file does not
exist: modules/nf-core/gunzip/environment.yml".

Fix: switch to the `${moduleDir}` variable which resolves to the module's
own directory regardless of invocation cwd. This is the pattern used by
every other nf-core module I've inspected (rnaseq, methylseq, smrnaseq).

Affected modules:
 - modules/nf-core/custom/tabulartogseagct/main.nf
 - modules/nf-core/geoquery/getgeo/main.nf
 - modules/nf-core/gunzip/main.nf
 - modules/nf-core/rmarkdownnotebook/main.nf
 - modules/nf-core/untar/main.nf
 - modules/nf-core/zip/main.nf

Verified on Ares 2026-04-21: before patch, pipeline crashed at GUNZIP_GTF
in ~5s; after patch, pipeline advances past gunzip stage.

Backups at `<file>.orig.pre-mtang-patch` next to each modified file.

To upstream: PR at https://github.com/nf-core/differentialabundance against
each of the six module files.

--- modules/nf-core/custom/tabulartogseagct/main.nf.orig.pre-mtang-patch	2026-04-21 18:31:22.639052484 -0500
+++ modules/nf-core/custom/tabulartogseagct/main.nf	2026-04-21 18:31:22.667052514 -0500
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
     tag "$meta.id"
     label 'process_single'
 
-    conda 'modules/nf-core/custom/tabulartogseagct/environment.yml'
+    conda "${moduleDir}/environment.yml"
     container "${ workflow.containerEngine == 'singularity' && !task.ext.singularity_pull_docker_container ?
         'https://depot.galaxyproject.org/singularity/ubuntu:20.04' :
         'nf-core/ubuntu:20.04' }"
